# oracle: pair_style meam, single element diamond reference (w15meam_dia_lib.meam + w15meam_dia.meam, zbl 0), 2x2x2 diamond cells (64 atoms), lattice constant 5.0 A (nearest-neighbour distance re = sqrt(3)/4 a), 0.02 A sinusoidal displacement, velocities from atom-style variables, fix nve, 50 steps of 0.001 ps
# oracle: the diamond reference has 4 nearest neighbours at re = 2.165 A, 12 second neighbours at 3.54 A (screened to zero in the perfect crystal) and 12 third neighbours at 4.146 A; the 0.02 A displacements keep every pair distance in [2.0, 4.06] A, so no pair enters the cutoff smoothing window [3.9, 4.0] A (the window form is not verified, see the meam15 report)
# oracle-inputs: w15meam_dia_lib.meam w15meam_dia.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-6 abs=1e-9
# oracle-tolerance: pe, press and the per-atom state agree within rel=1e-6 with the tabulated pair term (native pair table of 1000 intervals over [0, 1.1 rc], see meam.ts); the earlier press offset of 5e-6 was the analytic pair term forces
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         diamond 5.0
region          box block 0 2 0 2 0 2
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 28.09
variable        dx atom 0.02*sin(2.3*x+1.1*y+0.4*z)
variable        dy atom 0.02*cos(1.9*y-0.7*x+0.3*z)
variable        dz atom 0.02*sin(1.3*z+0.8*x-0.5*y)
displace_atoms  all move v_dx v_dy v_dz units box
variable        vx atom 0.4*cos(1.7*y-0.6*z)
variable        vy atom 0.4*sin(1.2*z+0.9*x)
variable        vz atom 0.3*cos(2.1*x-0.8*y+0.2)
velocity        all set v_vx v_vy v_vz units box
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w15meam_dia_lib.meam W w15meam_dia.meam W
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve
thermo          10
thermo_style    custom step pe press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
run             50
